                        


Item #: SCP-5083 

Object Class: Safe 

Special Containment Procedures:  No special safety procedures are to be taken with SCP-5083 due to its generally calm and docile behavior and its ability to do as it is told and not break rules or cause trouble for the most part. SCP-5083 is still not allowed to enter restricted areas or leave Site-19 despite its cooperation and behavior due to SCP-5083’s curiosity commonly overwhelming it leading to it attempting to interact with Euclid and Keter class SCP items and attempting to get back to the outside world.

Description:  SCP-5083 is a thirteen (13) year old caucasian male measuring 1.5 meters in height and approximately 95.2 lbs. SCP-5083 spends most of the day playing video games and listening to music. SCP-5083 claims to not feel pain and that it can heal itself almost instantly regardless of the type of damage whether it be a cut, burn, stab wound, gunshot, sprain, a broken bone, fracture, and electrocution among other things. SCP-5083 also claims that it doesn’t need to eat or drink but that it does anyway and testing proves that SCP-5083 is telling the truth. SCP-5083 was found in Kernersville, North Carolina outside of an apartment building after a woman called 911 because she claimed to have seen a child slit his own throat after getting into a fight with another child. However, the woman claimed that the first child did not react and only had a wound for a split second before he started to laugh as he noticed the other child’s horrified expression. SCP-5083 was brought into Foundation custody to be questioned as soon as it was found and the woman and the other child were both given Class-A amnestics. This file will be updated once an interview with SCP-5083 has taken place.

                    

                                    





            
    

                    



                    

                    
                    
                        
